hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1378","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “He rode The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was riding with him soon, and he did not come until the sun had eclipsed, so I went out with some women and we were in front of the room, so he came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, quickly got off his boat, and the one who was praying stood in his place, and the people stood up behind him, so he said “Allahu Akbar,” and stood for a long time, then bowed. He bowed for a long time, then he rose, then he stood and stood for a long time, which was short of the first standing, then he bowed and prolonged the bowing, which was short of the first bowing, then He rose, then prostrated, prolonging the prostration, then he rose, then prostrated, prostrating without the first prostration, then he rose, prolonging the standing, and it was short of the first standing, then He bowed and prolonged the bowing, which was less than the first bowing, then he rose and stood and stood for a long time, which was less than the first bowing, then he bowed and prolonged the bowing, He did not perform the first bowing, then he prostrated and left. His prayer consisted of four rak’ahs in four prostrations, so he sat down and the sun had risen.” Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, the same"
